Dragon Burst 0192: what the PC SDK (Burst Limit Recompiled v7.3, rexglue-sdk burstlimit 3c41e4b) added since this port's base (465f9ef) that applies to Android

From the PC, adapted where this SDK differs:
- e6fabfb: the VSync worker no longer fires vblanks forever when the guest clock reads a tick lower than before (an
  interrupt storm), and after a long stall catches up 8 vblanks, not the whole backlog; input_poll_on_read (default
  on): the controllers are read when the game asks for them (up to a frame less input delay); the latency probe
  (latency_log, debug; present= is the frames shown here).
- 9dbb755 (Android variant): the VSync worker sleeps to 0.2 ms before each vblank with nanosleep (microsecond
  precise on Linux) instead of yield-spinning the last 2 ms (~12% of a core at 60 Hz); the PC uses a waitable timer.
- 40f162f: the profile is signed in on one movable user index (a pad on user 1-3 still sees Xbox LIVE).
- a126623 (without the PC quick menu part): achievement unlocks kept per profile, the old file moved there once.
- 92eed19 (without the D3D12 texture cache): texture packs: premultiplied alpha, images over 8192 downscaled, mips
  that follow the game's, the RAM budget for async loads, ARGB-swizzled k_8_8_8_8 colours.
- b5ef429 (without the Wine proxy): the UI watchdog (ui_watchdog) logs where the UI thread is stuck for 5 s+.
- 0cac967 (only hid_generic_mapping; the keyboard play is PC only): controllers SDL has no mapping for get a
  generic gamepad layout instead of being ignored.
- 37734bb: input_test_pads (idle virtual pads for tests); fa21d55: the gpu_state console command (host presents =
  the frames shown here) and the draws_focus GPU profile pass.

Left out (PC only): D3D12 and its native renderer (the Renut is Android's), DLSS, adapters, the PC quick menu,
keyboard and mouse, the WinHTTP lobby, the display-locked vblank and present pacing of the PC presenter (c4db5a3),
643fdda (0007 already skips the protection query on Android).

